{
  "name": "Rodrigo R. Granjel",
  "shortBio": "Integrating experiments and theory to study how species interactions shape community stability and function.",
  "biography": [
    "My research combines ecological theory and empirical data to understand how abiotic conditions and interactions between species shape plant communities.",
    "I completed my PhD at the University of Sevilla, where I studied how nutrient availability and multiple species interactions determine the ability of plants to coexist.",
    "As a Fulbright research fellow at North Carolina State University, I investigated species interactions and the stability and functioning of microbial communities associated with the pitcher plant Sarracenia purpurea. My research experience also includes institutions in Brazil, Sweden, and Switzerland.",
    "My wider interests include biodiversity and stability, chemical ecology, soil ecology, and ecosystem functioning."
  ],
